         covers='About 38 years, from Sinai to the plains of Moab',
         summary="Numbers follows Israel from Sinai to the edge of Canaan, a journey of weeks that took nearly forty years. After the tribes are counted and organized, the people set out, but grumbling turns into rebellion when they refuse to enter the land at Kadesh (13–14). That generation dies in the wilderness. Along the way come Korah's revolt, Moses' own failure at Meribah, the bronze snake, and Balaam, who is hired to curse Israel and can only bless. A second census counts the new generation, ready on the plains of Moab.",
         themes=['Unbelief and its cost', "God's faithfulness to an unfaithful people", "God's presence leading the camp", 'A new generation and a second chance'],
