         covers='About a month on the plains of Moab, ending with Moses\' death',
         summary="Deuteronomy is Moses' farewell: three sermons to the generation about to enter Canaan. He retells their history, repeats and applies the law for life in the land, and calls them to love the LORD with all their heart. The book is shaped like an ancient treaty between a great king and his people, with history, terms, blessings and curses, and witnesses. It ends with Moses' song and blessing, his view of the land from Mount Nebo, and his death.",
         themes=["Love and loyalty to the one God (the Shema, 6:4–5)", "Remember: don't forget what God has done", 'Obedience brings life; disobedience, exile', 'Choose life (30:19)'],
